---
import "../styles/global.css";
interface Props { title: string }
const { title } = Astro.props;
const REPO = "https://github.com/tbrunsting/Transfer-Market-Efficiency";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Which clubs in Europe's top five leagues get the most on-field value per euro spent in the transfer market, 2017/18 to 2023/24." />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="wrap">
      <slot />
      <!-- One footer for both pages: the page adds its own note, the credits are always the same,
           and because this sits outside <main> it survives the pages' fetch-failure state. -->
      <footer>
        <p class="page-note"><slot name="notes" /></p>
        <h2 class="credits-head">Data &amp; sources</h2>
        <p class="credits">
          Transfer fees, market values, squads and club crests come from
          <a href="https://www.transfermarkt.com/">Transfermarkt</a>, via its public club transfer
          pages and the <a href="https://github.com/dcaribou/transfermarkt-datasets">transfermarkt-datasets</a>
          project. Player minutes and performance come from <a href="https://fbref.com/">FBref</a>
          (Opta era), through the archived
          <a href="https://github.com/JaseZiv/worldfootballR_data">worldfootballR_data</a> snapshot.
          Shot-creating actions come from the Kaggle dataset
          <a href="https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/akshankrithick/fbref-2017-2024-for-europes-top-5-leagues">FBref
          2017–2024 for Europe's top 5 leagues</a>. Club cities and seventeen cup editions come from
          <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/">Wikidata</a>. None of these sources endorses or has
          reviewed this project. Club crests are trademarks of their respective owners, shown for
          identification only.
        </p>
        <p class="credits">
          <strong>The scores are derived, not reported.</strong> The Transfer Efficiency Score, its four
          pillars and every z-score on these pages are calculated by this project from the sources above. No source publishes them, and they are one defensible way of
          measuring efficiency rather than the way.
        </p>
        <p class="credits">
          <strong>This is a frozen snapshot, not a live feed.</strong> Seven seasons, 2017/18 to 2023/24,
          exported once from a local warehouse; the generation date is shown above. Fees and valuations at
          each source may since have changed, and undisclosed fees are counted but never estimated.
          <a href={`${REPO}#readme`}>Method, limitations and full source code</a>.
        </p>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
